  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Qt: Parent GeometryStateDialogs when setting them modal",
  "description": "On Linux with Mutter (and possibly other window managers), dialogs\nwithout a parent aren't always on top, even if ApplicationModal.\nOn Windows, dialogs that are applicationModal are always on top,\neven if orphan, but setting the parent adds a few effects like causing\nthe appropriate dialog to shake when the user tries to click in the\nblocked parent.\n\nWe don't set the parent normally when creating a GSD (so that it\nwon't be always on top), but do so when we make it modal (so that it\nwill be.)\n\nFix #19099",
